Z||000007||JIM GOOSE||10-07-1999||11:15 AM|||| I have an IFG twin-turbo system that intend to install on my car at some future point. I spent too much money upfront on my project & came up alittle short in the rear. Rebuilt my engine completely w forged pistons, crank was nitrided & meta-laxed,pan plumbed for oil drains-both sides. These are water-cooled turbos as used on Chrysler 2.2( bout a zillion of these around)& dont have wastegates. Press. supposedly controlled by a pop-off valve that mounts opposite the throttlebody. I got a good buy on this setup which had not been used but think the turbos are rebuilts. Just putting a turbo on the engine is only a small part of the deal,theres lots of plumbing involved, waterlines,oillines,exhaust pipes. Then you come to fuel mgmt-right airfuel ratio for the boost as it comes up. IFG supplies a chip thats supposed to enrich the mix and retard the timing. Have a YAMAHA SECA TURBO mcycle thats a good model for turbosystem but of course doesnt have a computer. It has carbs and a rising rate press reg. that keeps the fuel press. 3psi above boost. Anyway, I could go on & on.   JMSG||||reg||1
Z||000008||88 Fiero||10-07-1999||03:42 PM||||Jim... just word of advice...be careful in installing the twin turbo from IFG..In other words they don't work...I had a buddy that bought the single turbo from IFG and it blew his engine...That company don't know anything about turbo except kit cars and V8 engine..Talk to alot of people with this kit and very much hate...Settle with Desing One Systems..this has been proven by Kevin Leslie in which the same guy who design the Turbo for Miller Woods. Did you check if the Twin Turbo Kit is complete... I bet you not all of the parts that you need is in the kit... Your gonna wind up calling them and delay your project...I will find an article of a guy who bought an IFG Twin Turbo Kit and his experience dealing with IFG when he was installing the kit and I'll scan that and email it to you..Also if you notice the Air intake charge is located above the exhaust manifold of the car...Now, how do you suppose to get cold air inside the turbo where your going to draw hot air coming from the exhaust manifold...that's a problem. You better study this kit first before you install it....||||reg||1
Z||000009||Greg Piet||10-07-1999||03:52 PM||||What about the kit Stroker said he was making up which would be 1/2 the price of design one? <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/000139.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/000139.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
