Z||000012||SCCA FIERO||10-07-1999||10:07 PM||||I have the brochure for the I.F.G. Twin Turbo....looks cool.<P>I have also been building a turbo for my Fiero and so far have the turbo, Y pipe, and the drain installed in my oilpan. My turbo came from a 87 T-bird and is an IHI unit and is water cooled. Total cost to me so far...50 bucks. I still need a few more things but I plan to stay under 1000 dollars.<P>I have also called Design One for the possibilty of buying their plumbing and things...no go.||||reg||4
Z||000013||TOM||10-07-1999||11:42 PM|||| Who made your piping?||||reg||1
Z||000014||SCCA FIERO||10-08-1999||01:19 AM||||My pipes were made by a guy I do not know. He made them for a friend and he gave them to my friend who gave them to me. I have tried to track down the person that made this Y pipe, but no luck. They are 1 3/4 inch with a bracket for the EGR and a springy part of pipe in it for flexing. These pipes are very well made and are stainless steel. I have taken these pipes to a local muffler/speed shop and he has never seen the flexing pipe in this Y pipe. <P>I plan to park my Fiero at the end of this month for the winter and hopefully will get the turbo installed.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||JIM GOOSE||10-08-1999||10:40 AM||||I'm aware of IFG's asst. lawsuits and their reputation & the kit I have is pretty much complete. I got it from a guy who had been into Fiero based kit cars & he had two kits, one for auto.,one for manual & it was a good buy. Anybody that sticks a turbo on an engine and doesnt pay attention to his air-fuel ratio is risking a holed piston,doesnt matter if its IFG or anyone else. I've been a student of turbocharging & supercharging for at least 15 years, have rebuilt turbos & probably have most books ever written about them. As I said, have a turbo motorcycle which is a very good aid to learning the mechanics of a system. I would not even crank the engine of my car without having an air-fuel gauge or exhaust temp,maybe both,also boost & fuel pressure. I bgt this kit for the basics which are there,with the admission that I alone would be responsible if the engine blows. Also,you cannot blame Design One or any other kit maker for not wanting to give away secrets they have worked to perfect. I'm familiar with D-1's setup that works musch like a stock Buick GN w map sensor & chip combo. As said prev. arising rate regulator-boost sensitive can be used to richen the mix w port inj. used on Fiero.  The whole turbo thing is a favorite subject with FIERO people cause we think it would make the car so much better||||reg||1
Z||000016||88 Fiero||10-08-1999||01:02 PM||||Jim are you thinking that I dont agree about having the Fiero Turbocharge. If you are, then your wrong...I already have a Design One/Miller Woods Turbo Kit  Stage 4 sitting in my garage.. I will be rebuilding my engine next year and will be going to a 3.4 block... I am also aquiring another GT Fiero for the purpose of having it with a Northstar Engine with it...||||reg||1
